"Stabwound" <exhumed@REMOVE-THISgmailDELETE-THIS.com> wrote in message news:<10iidnlq1rkil94@corp.supernews.com>...
> I was looking through the defaults.nh file and I noticed there is a section
> for changing the colors of the windows. What exactly is the syntax you are
> supposed to use here? I am looking to change the background of the
> status/message bars to black, and the text to white or yellow. I messed
> around with it but the best I could do is make black text on black
> background for the message box, and that's it.

There is an example in defaults.nh that shows the format. the format is like this:
OPTIONS=windowcolors:status fgcolor/bgcolor message fgcolor/bgcolor

So, in your case that would be:

OPTIONS=windowcolors:status yellow/trueblack message yellow/trueblack

(Notice that you can use 'black' to get the color of black monsters, which
is dark grey, or 'trueblack' for true black.)
